print(size, capacity)
```
wrong[3 3]: The capacity doubles when the array is full: 1 → 2 → 4, so it skips 3.
wrong[3 8]: The 3rd append finds size 2 and capacity 2, so it grows to 4. Nothing grows it again.
wrong[4 4]: There are 3 appends, so the size is 3.
