wrong: (1, 1), then (2, 2), then (3, 4).

=== task: multi easy
title: Cheap on a dynamic array
prompt: Choose **every** operation on a dynamic array that is O(1), or O(1) amortized.
* Reading item i :: Right. Address arithmetic, as in any array.
* Writing item i :: Right. O(1).
* Appending at the end :: Right. O(1) amortized: growing is rare enough to average out.
* Removing the last item :: Right. Nothing has to move.
- Inserting at index 0 :: Every item shifts right: O(n).
- Searching for a value in an unsorted array :: O(n): the items are checked one by one.
hint: Which ones work at one slot, or at the end?
hint: Four of them are.
right: Reads, writes, appends and pops from the end are cheap. Inserting at the front and searching touch every item.
wrong: O(1): read, write, append (amortized), pop from the end. O(n): insert at the front and search.

